# Figma → portfolio data mapping

Use this workflow whenever Figma is the source of truth for a project case study (copy, section structure, captions, asset filenames in brackets).

## 1. Resolve URL and fetch design context

- From `https://www.figma.com/design/:fileKey/...?node-id=456-22574`:
  - **`fileKey`**: the segment after `/design/` (use **branch key** if the URL uses `/branch/:branchKey/`).
  - **`nodeId`**: convert `456-22574` → `456:22574`.
- Before calling Figma MCP tools, **read the tool descriptor** under the workspace MCP folder (e.g. `mcps/user-Figma/tools/get_design_context.json`) for required parameters.
- Call **`get_design_context`** with `fileKey` and `nodeId` (and optional `clientLanguages` / `clientFrameworks` for logging).
- Treat returned React/Tailwind (and screenshots) as **reference for copy and hierarchy only**. Do **not** paste Tailwind into this repo; encode everything as **`Project` / `SectionBlock` data** and existing components ([`SectionBlockView`](src/components/project/section-block/section-block.tsx), [`ProjectMediaBlock`](src/components/project/media-block/media-block.tsx)).

## 2. Map the top frame → `Project`

Align the header area of the frame with [`Project`](src/data/projects.ts):

| Figma (typical) | `Project` field |
|-------------------|-----------------|
| Title | `name` |
| Short line / card blurb | `description` |
| Intro paragraph(s) | `intro` |
| Role / Year / Contribution table | `role`, `year`, `contribution` (same labels as [`InfoTable`](src/components/project/info-table) on [`ProjectDetail`](src/components/project-detail/project-detail.tsx)) |
| Thumbnail / hero art | `image`, and extend `images` for card carousel when needed |
| Brand accent (color or OKLCH gradient) | `accent`; optional `accentDark` for dark theme |

Paths under `public/` become web paths by stripping `public`: e.g. `public/images/projects/foo/bar.png` → `/images/projects/foo/bar.png`.

## 3. Map vertical sections → `sections`

Each major stacked block in Figma ≈ one **`ProjectSection`** with **`blocks: SectionBlock[]`**:

| Figma pattern | `SectionBlock` |
|---------------|----------------|
| Large gradient section title | `{ type: 'heading', text: '…' }` |
| Body copy (one or more paragraphs) | `{ type: 'text', text: '…' }` or `text: ['…', '…']` |
| Media frame + caption / toolbar | `{ type: 'media', media: … }` |

Order **`blocks`** top-to-bottom as in Figma (heading → text → media → …).

## 4. Carousels (`1 / 2`, `1 / 3`, arrows)

When Figma shows **multiple slides with one caption area** or a counter like **`1 / N`**:

- Use **one** media section block with **`media` as an array**: `media: [ slide1, slide2, … ]`.
- Each slide is one **`MediaBlock`** (`type: 'image' | 'video'`) with its **`label`** set to **that slide’s** caption text.

[`ProjectMediaBlock`](src/components/project/media-block/media-block.tsx) shows **`active.label`** for the current index, so split Figma copy **per slide**, not one giant string for the whole carousel (unless it is a single non-gallery asset).

## 5. Bracket filenames in caption text

Designers often embed asset hints: `[ev-stats.png]`, `[clip.mp4]`, `[empty-image.png]`.

- Resolve the basename to a **web `src`** under **`public/`**, usually **`/images/projects/<slug>/…`** for project-owned assets.
- **Strip** the `[…]` segment from the **`label`** string shown in the UI (keep labels readable).
- **`[empty-image.png]`** → **`/images/projects/shared/empty-image.png`** (shared placeholder).
- If Figma names a file that **does not exist** in the repo, prefer the shared empty image (or ask the user to add the file); note the mismatch in the PR/summary.

## 6. `MediaBlock` flags

- **`cover: true`**: use when the frame should read as full-bleed / cover (match sibling projects and Figma intent).
- **`type: 'video'`**: `.mp4`, `.webm`, etc.; **`loop`** defaults in [`ProjectVideo`](src/components/project/media-block/media-block.tsx) unless you need `loop: false`.
- **`scale`**: only on video when a clip needs scaling (rare; see existing entries in [`projects.ts`](src/data/projects.ts)).

## 7. Spacing

- **Do not** encode top spacing on media via data. **`ProjectMediaBlock`** applies **fixed top padding** on the frame wrapper in CSS ([`media-block.module.css`](src/components/project/media-block/media-block.module.css)); there is **no** `spacer` field on section blocks.

## 8. Finish

- Update **[`src/data/projects.ts`](src/data/projects.ts)** (and place new assets under **`public/images/projects/<slug>/`** when applicable).
- Run **`npm run build`** and fix TypeScript errors.

## Out of scope (unless asked)

- Figma Code Connect / automatic component mapping.
- Downloading binary assets from short-lived Figma MCP asset URLs; prefer files already in **`public/`**.

